   100	of the L2-norm of weights over the L2-norm of gradients. Intuitively, this offers a major beneﬁt for
   101	large batch training. Such a normalization provides robustness to exploding and vanishing gradients
   102	since the trust ratio explicitly compares the magnitudes of the weights and the gradients for each layer.
   103	Exploding gradients occur due to signiﬁcantly large gradients compared to the weights. Therefore,
   104	the trust ratio will adapt to produce a small value to lower the LR, reducing the chance of divergence.
   105	The corresponding effect happens for vanishing gradients.
