   214	4.2 Accumulating Model Updates with Momentum
   215	Using momentum on top of SGD has proven to have great success in accelerating network training
   216	by a running accumulation of the gradient history to dampen oscillations. This seems particularly
   217	relevant for FL where participating parties may have a sparse distribution of data, and hold a limited
   218	subset of labels. In this subsection we test the effect of momentum at the server on the performance
   219	of FedAvg.
