   806	Experimental Setup. For the synthetic experiment, we consider a setup with 20 clients, 30 samples
   807	at each client, and model size to be 1000, making this an overparameterized problem. The data at each
   808	client is generated following a similar procedure as the synthetic dataset in Li et al. (2020). We use
   809	the federated version of EMNIST available at Caldas et al. (2019), which is naturally partitioned into
   810	3400 clients. For CIFAR-10/100 we artiﬁcally partition the data into 100 clients, and for CINIC-10
   811	we partition the data into 200 clients. In both cases, we follow a Dirichlet distribution withα = 0.3
   812	for the partitioning to model heterogeneity among client data (Hsu et al., 2019). For EMNIST we use
   813	the same CNN architecture used in Reddi et al. (2021). For CIFAR10, CIFAR100 and CINIC-10
   814	we use a ResNet-18 model (He et al., 2016). For our baselines, we ﬁnd the best performing ηg
   815	andηl by grid-search tuning. For FedExP we optimize for ϵ andηl by grid search. We ﬁx the
   816	number of participating clients to 20, minibatch size to 50 and number of local updates to 20 for all
   817	experiments. In Appendix D, we provide additional details and results, including the best performing
   818	hyperparameters, comparison with FedProx (Li et al., 2020), and results for more rounds.
   819	FedExP comprehensively outperforms FedAvg and baselines. Our experimental results in
   820	Figure 3 demonstrate that FedExP clearly outperforms FedAvg and competing baselines that use
   821	the best performingηg andηl found by grid search. Moreover, FedExP does not require additional
   822	communication or storage at clients or server unlike SCAFFOLD and FedAdagrad. The order-
   823	wise improvement in the case of the convex linear regression experiment conﬁrms our theoretical
   824	motivation for FedExP outlined in Section 3.2. In this case, since (6) is satisﬁed, we know that the
   825	FedExP iterates are always moving towards the optimum. For realistic FL tasks, we see a consistent
