   300	4.2.2 Personalized Momentum Calculation
   301	At each round r, the server computes the personalized momentum for each selected client k by:
   302	∆k
   303	r = ∆ r + αr
   304	1 − αr
   305	ck, (1)
   306	where ∆r is the global momentum, αr is the momentum factor, and ck is the local correction for
   307	client k. This step ensures the alignment of the global and local updates. The coefﬁcient αr
   308	1−αr
   309	arises
   310	because, during the local updates, the momentum term is combined with the gradient as:
   311	vr
   312	b+1,k = αr gr
   313	b,k + (1 − αr) ∆k
   314	r . (2)
   315	We want the correction term ck to affect the gradient gr
   316	b,k directly, so the coefﬁcient αr
   317	1−αr
   318	is used
   319	to scale ck in the global momentum computation. This adjustment ensures that ck has the same
   320	effect on the gradient as it would in the local update, enabling a consistent blend of global and local
   321	dynamics in the personalized momentum. This transformation decouples the correction term from
   322	momentum, reducing the need to transmit separate vectors for momentum and correction and saving
