  2070	B.3 Limitation Analysis
  2071	Dataset-Speciﬁc Sensitivity of λ. The choice of the decay factor λ, which governs the update
  2072	dynamics of αr, plays a critical role in training stability and performance. However, our ﬁndings
  2073	suggest that the optimal value of λ may vary across different datasets and distribution settings. This
  2074	sensitivity could pose challenges for practitioners seeking to apply the method in diverse real-world
  2075	scenarios, as it introduces an additional layer of hyperparameter tuning.
  2076	Instability Caused by Cosine Similarity Fluctuations. The use of Mean Cosine Similarity as an
  2077	indicator of training-phase progression enables adaptive momentum adjustment. Nevertheless, this
  2078	metric exhibits signiﬁcant short-term ﬂuctuations, which may lead to unstable or overly aggressive

