   277	2020; Khanduri et al. 2021), while ignoring many other mo-
   278	mentum schemes that outperform SHB in many non-FL set-
   279	tings.
   280	In order to systematically understand the role of server
   281	momentum schemes in FL, we propose a new algo-
   282	rithm which we refer to as Federated General Momentum
   283	(FedGM). FedGM replaces the ServerOPT xt+1 = xt− ∆ t
   284	in FedAvg with the following,
   285	dt+1 = (1− β )∆ t + βd t, h t+1 = (1− ν)∆ t + νdt+1,
   286	xt+1 = xt− ηht+1.
   287	(2)
   288	where the hyperparameter set H = {η, β, ν }. η is server
   289	learning rate, β and ν are two hyperparameters which we
   290	call momentum factor and instant discount factor.
   291	By setting ν as 0, FedGM becomes FedAvg with two-
   292	sided learning rates (Y ang, Fang, and Liu 2021), i.e., choices
   293	of η other than 1 is allowed, which we refer to as FedSGD.
   294	By setting ν = 1 , FedGM becomes FedAvgM (Hsu, Qi,
   295	and Brown 2019) (or FedSHB), which essentially applies
   296	server SHB, i.e. we update the model by a “momentum
   297	buffer” dt+1. β controls how slowly the momentum buffer
   298	is updated. FedGM could be interpreted as a ν-weighted av-
   299	erage of the FedAvgM update step and the plain FedAvg
   300	update step. ν is thus referred to as instant discount factor.
   301	FedGM leverages the general formulation of QHM (Ma
   302	and Y arats 2019) and is much more general than just
   303	FedAvg and FedAvgM. It subsumes many other momen-
   304	tum variants that are never explored in FL. For exam-
   305	ple, if ν = β , FedGM becomes a new algorithm which
   306	can be naturally referred to as FedNAG, i.e. application
   307	of the popular optimizer Nesterov’s accelerated gradient
   308	(NAG) to FL. Speciﬁcally, we update model by xt+1 =
   309	xt− η [(1− β )∆ t + βd t+1], where dt+1 is the momentum
   310	buffer.
   311	FedGM could further recover the FL version of many
   312	other momentum schemes, e.g., SNV (Lessard, Recht, and
   313	Packard 2014), PID (An et al. 2018), ASGD (Kidambi et al.
   314	2018), and Triple Momentum (V an Scoy, Freeman, and
   315	Lynch 2018), with different η, β, ν . Therefore, FedGM de-
   316	scribes a family of momentum schemes, most of which have
   317	not been studied yet in FL.
